---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';

/** Agent setup: how machines read this documentation honestly. */
const base = 'https://bitcoinuniverseio.github.io/docs-stampdex';
const snippets = [
  {
    name: 'llms.txt',
    body: 'Point an agent at the index of the corpus. It lists every page with its address and purpose.',
    code: `${base}/llms.txt`,
  },
  {
    name: 'Full corpus',
    body: 'One Markdown document containing every page, with source verification records preserved.',
    code: `${base}/llms-full.txt`,
  },
  {
    name: 'Page index (JSON)',
    body: 'A compact machine index: id, title, description, content type, audience, risk level, and the Markdown address of each page.',
    code: `${base}/index.json`,
  },
  {
    name: 'Per-page Markdown',
    body: 'Every page has a clean Markdown representation at /markdown/<id>. The View as Markdown action on each page links to it.',
    code: `${base}/markdown/concepts/custody`,
  },
  {
    name: 'OpenAPI document',
    body: 'The public API contract, generated in the application repository and snapshotted here. Discoverable also at /.well-known/api-catalog.',
    code: `${base}/api/downloads/openapi.json`,
  },
];
const mcp = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "stampdex-docs": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@bitcoinuniverse/stampdex-docs-mcp"],
      "env": { "DOCSDIR": "/path/to/docs-stampdex/dist" }
    }
  }
}`;
const claude = `In Claude Code, add the MCP server with the configuration above, then ask:

  What does StampDEX say about where my BTC sits while an SRC-20 trade settles?

The honest answer comes from stampdex_docs_get_section with id concepts/custody;
check that every claim the agent makes traces to a page it can cite.`;
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Agent setup',
    description: 'How to point AI agents, coding assistants, and MCP clients at the StampDEX documentation: corpus files, page index, OpenAPI, and the read-only MCP server.',
  }}
>
  <p class="sd-api-lede">
    Machines get the same facts humans get, in the same shapes, with the same
    source records. Agents must cite pages, admit when the documentation does
    not answer, and never present an unreleased feature as live. Nothing here
    can trade, sign, or move funds: the MCP server is read-only by
    construction.
  </p>

  <h2>Corpus files</h2>
  {
    snippets.map((snippet) => (
      <div class="sd-agent-file">
        <h3>{snippet.name}</h3>
        <p>{snippet.body}</p>
        <div class="sd-scroll">
          <pre><code>{snippet.code}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))
  }

  <h2>MCP server</h2>
  <p>
    <code>@bitcoinuniverse/stampdex-docs-mcp</code> is a versioned, read-only
    MCP package. Tools:{' '}
    <code>
      stampdex_docs_search, stampdex_docs_get_page, stampdex_docs_get_section,
      stampdex_docs_get_api_operation, stampdex_docs_get_release,
      stampdex_docs_get_capability, stampdex_docs_get_wallet_support,
      stampdex_docs_get_screenshot_evidence
    </code>
    . It serves a built copy of this site, so the tools answer from the same
    snapshot a reader sees.
  </p>
  <div class="sd-scroll">
    <pre><code>{mcp}</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2>Example: Claude Code</h2>
  <div class="sd-scroll">
    <pre><code>{claude}</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2>Exact limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The server is read-only. There is no tool that writes, signs, or broadcasts.</li>
    <li>It serves the built documentation only; private repositories are unreachable.</li>
    <li>Release claims are only as current as the build it serves; verify with <code>GET /api/version</code>.</li>
    <li>Prices and predictions are out of scope everywhere on this site, including here.</li>
  </ul>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
  .sd-api-lede {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--sd-muted);
    max-width: 46rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .sd-agent-file {
    margin: 1.1rem 0;
  }
  .sd-agent-file h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.2rem;
  }
  .sd-agent-file p {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--sd-muted);
  }
  pre {
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-code-rule);
    border-radius: var(--sd-r-md);
    background: var(--sd-code-bg);
    padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--sd-mono);
    font-size: 0.82em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
</style>
